## SDKs — install + connect + first call

Pick the developer's language. Default data target `localhost:50051` (plaintext
in dev). **Set `authTarget` too whenever the app uses auth/native services.**
Current release baseline is **UDB 0.5.0** with wire protocol **1.0.0**; keep the
broker and SDK package on the same product version unless deliberately testing
compatibility. The platform-service wave (Vault, Metering, Scheduler, Search,
Webhook, Workflow, Lock, LiveQuery, Config, Backup, Embedding) and the
consistency/idempotency contract below shipped in 0.4.x and are stable in 0.5.0.

**New for consumers in 0.5.0** (behavior changes — read before upgrading from
0.4.x): **(1) Soft-delete is now the default read scope** — on a table annotated
`soft_delete`, `Delete` tombstones the row (idempotent `UPDATE`, not a physical
delete) and ordinary `Select`/list results EXCLUDE tombstoned rows automatically;
there is no wire flag to re-expose them. **(2) Opaque row-revision (ETag) CAS** —
reads can return an opaque `revision`, and `Update`/`Delete` (and the new `BulkCas`)
accept `expected_revision` for optimistic concurrency even when your proto has no
`version` column. **(3) `BulkCas`** on the DataBroker — a bounded, tenant-scoped
batch of conditional single-row updates in one tx; a per-item CAS miss is reported
as `conflicted` (not a whole-batch failure) so a partial retry with the same
`idempotency_key` is safe. **(4) Storage hard-delete** — `DeleteFile` takes a
`DeleteMode` (`SOFT` tombstone vs `HARD` durable byte GC); and register-established
`is_public`/size are IMMUTABLE at finalize (a mismatch is a typed
`FAILED_PRECONDITION`). **(5) Page tokens are query-bound** — reusing a page token
under a different filter/sort/fields returns `FAILED_PRECONDITION`, so always page
the SAME query. **(6) Idempotency is input-bound** — replaying a key with different
inputs returns `FAILED_PRECONDITION`, not a bogus success. **(7) Enterprise
`udb deploy`** — a declarative `udb.deploy.yaml` + `udb deploy plan|apply|render`
turns minimum args into a full production env (mTLS/JWT/RLS/audit) and idempotently
bootstraps tenants/service-accounts/grants/api-keys/policies.

### TypeScript / Node — `@udb_plus/sdk`
```bash
npm i @udb_plus/sdk@0.5.0
```
```ts
import { dataBrokerClient, metadata, UdbMetadata } from "@udb_plus/sdk/client";

const meta: UdbMetadata = {
  tenantId: "acme", projectId: "billing", userId: "user-1",
  purpose: "web.request", scopes: ["udb:read", "udb:write"],
  serviceIdentity: "billing.api",
};
const broker = dataBrokerClient("localhost:50051");
broker.Select({ message_type: "shop.v1.Customer", limit: 50 }, metadata(meta),
  (err, rs) => console.log(rs?.records));
```
Entry points: `@udb_plus/sdk/client` (DataBroker + `metadata()`),
`@udb_plus/sdk/auth` (`UdbAuthClient`), `@udb_plus/sdk` (full `UdbProject`
facade — configure `{ target, authTarget, credentials: { bearerToken | apiKey } }`).
Adapters for Express / Fastify / Next.js under `adapters/`.

